vcl, sw, sd: ask the spooler only for printer metrics

Ely starts the kernel with SAL_DISABLE_PRINTERLIST and
SAL_DISABLE_DEFAULTPRINTER: on Windows each load asked the spooler
for the default printer, about 0.5 seconds (Ely SF.18). Ely prints
through PDF export. But a document that lays out by printer metrics
(Word's usePrinterMetrics, DOC's fUsePrinterMetrics, a Writer or
Impress PrinterIndependentLayout of DISABLED) then got a display
printer, and Writer and Impress fell back to the virtual device:
lines and pages broke differently.

A printer the document names read as not installed, so its
JobSetup was dropped too.

ely::AskPrinterQueues lifts both switches once. Looking up a named
printer calls it first. Writer calls it when
its reference device must be the printer, Impress when its layout
is printer-dependent; each drops the display printer made before.

